  "derived_from": [
    "src/tooluniverse/database_setup/embedding_database.py -- three handlers, each with one success return and bare {'error': ...} refusals.",
    "src/tooluniverse/database_setup/embedding_sync.py -- two handlers, same shape; the download handler adds {'error', 'missing', 'hint'} when the transfer leaves an artefact behind.",
    "src/tooluniverse/url_tool.py -- URLToPDFTextTool returns {fields.return_key: text} on success and {'status': 'error', 'error': ...} on every failure; this tool's config sets return_key to 'text'.",
    "src/tooluniverse/tool_finder_embedding.py -- find_tools has exactly two returns, picked by return_call_result.",
    "src/tooluniverse/tool_finder_llm.py -- same two, plus failure dicts of its own carrying success=False.",
    "src/tooluniverse/smolagent_tool.py -- run returns {'output', 'success': True, 'execution_time'} or {'output': None, 'success': False, 'error', 'error_type'}.",
    "src/tooluniverse/execute_function.py:prepare_tool_prompts -- returns a LIST of trimmed tool configs (name, description, parameter, required), which is why the finders answer an array."
  ],
  "how": "Derived from source, with one live reading. These classes each have a small enumerable set of returns, so the derivation is exhaustive where a live pass would be a lower bound. What could not be run here: the embedding stores and both tool finders need the `embedding`/`ml` extras, which this environment does not have -- Tool_RAG answered the framework's ToolServerError envelope instead; the two SmolAgent tools need smolagents and a model. get_webpage_text_from_url WAS run, on its own test example, and its error branch is the measured row below.",
  "the_stale_docstring": "ToolFinderEmbedding.find_tools documents its return as \"Tool prompts as a formatted string\". It is not a string: prepare_tool_prompts returns a list of dicts cut to name/description/parameter/required. A schema written from that docstring would have declared the wrong root type, which is why these were read from the code instead.",
  "invariant": "every payload under reachable validates against its tool's return_schema and exactly one oneOf branch matches it; every payload under unreachable validates against none",
